# Compiled output of src/*.java, plus resources/** staged next to it for the
# ServiceLoader vectors. run.sh opens every pass with `rm -rf "$BUILD"` and
# recompiles, so these files are pure build output. They were tracked until
# 2026-07-31, which meant merely running the suite deleted and recreated 45
# tracked files and left the worktree dirty — dangerous on a checkout with an
# auto-commit sweep, which could land .class files in a commit. Untracked with
# `git rm -r --cached regression-suite/build`; the files stay on disk.
build/

# Compiled output of the JDK-only named module (regression-suite/modules/).
# Regenerated by run.sh on every pass, exactly like build/.
build-modules/

# Transient directory run.sh uses to probe whether javac can target a given
# --release. Created and removed inside release_supported().
.release-probe.*

# Per-vector --jdk-only-report JSON, written when CRATONVM_ARGS names
# --jdk-only. PID-scoped (never a fixed shared name, unlike .guard-tmp) and
# removed by run.sh once the census summary has been printed. Ignored anyway,
# because a killed run leaves it behind and this checkout has an auto-commit
# sweep that would otherwise land a few hundred JSON files in a commit.
.jdk-only-reports.*
